Q: Google Apps Script HTML scriptlets trucates JSON object containing a single quote and a URL when using force-printing scriptlets A: <p>There is a chance you are not using the test deployment URL (.../dev) or that you haven't created a new version after making changes to your code and are still using the deployment URL (.../exec).</p>
<p>When looking to visualize the results on the client side of the changes made in the Apps Script project, I suggest you first use the test deployment URL. If everything is working correctly, create a new version for your current deployment and use the corresponding URL (.../exec) to confirm it.</p>
<hr />
<p>The following is working great for me</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function doGet(e) {
  const template = HtmlService.createTemplateFromFile('pageName');
  template.data = JSON.stringify({ &quot;time&quot;: &quot;2026-02-03T12:40:00.000Z&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;T'Challa&quot;, &quot;profileUrl&quot;: &quot;https://stackoverflow.com/users/23479790/brodblox09&quot; });
  return template.evaluate()
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;base target=&quot;_top&quot;&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;
  &lt;body&gt;
    &lt;script&gt;
    console.log(&lt;?!= data ?&gt;);
    &lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The Chrome DevTools console shows</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/nSjMsftP.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/nSjMsftP.png" alt="Chrome DevTools console screenshot" /></a></p>

Q: how to change content-security-policy frame-ancestors for a static webpage using iframes A: <p>Honestly speaking, you can't fix this.</p>
<p>The error is coming from <code>atlanta.xyz.org</code>, not your code. They've set a CSP that only allows their site to be embedded in iframes on <code>*.xyz.org</code> domains. Since you’re also loading your pages via <code>file://</code>, your container page doesn’t even have a valid origin that could be whitelisted</p>
<p>The easiest fix is to just open the external link in a new tab instead of trying to frame it:</p>
<pre><code>// Container Web page A
window.addEventListener('message', onMessageReceived);

function onMessageReceived(e) {
    const url = e.data;

    // You don't have to frame external URLs because of CSP
    if (typeof url === 'string' &amp;&amp; /^https?:\/\//.test(url)) {
        window.open(url, '_blank');
    } else {
        // You can frame content from the same origin or local content
        document.getElementById('post_page').src = url;
    }
}
</code></pre>

